{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause: debounce restarts its stability count only on a rising edge of noisy", "summary": "Design under investigation: [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1], approved and reviewed per [evidence:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.e1]. The work serves [requirement:req-19189b08df].\n\nObserved failure: the triage repro builds, reaches $finish at 175000 and reports 1 of 1 checks failed ([evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2], [run:run-0002]). VeriTriage gave only a weak classification: unknown_failure at 30% confidence, with 'Likely RTL bug' as its top hypothesis ([evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e1], [run:run-0001]). I treat that hypothesis as one candidate to test, not as a finding.\n\nSpecification: the header comment of the source fixes the behaviour. A change on noisy 'in either direction, restarts the count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never reaches clean'.\n\nDefect: in the RTL the count restarts only under `if (noisy && !prev) cnt <= 4'd0;`, which is a rising edge only. On a falling edge there is no restart. The count usually sits saturated at STABLE-1 after a long high, and the falling edge leaves it there. On the next edge, noisy==prev and cnt==STABLE-1 are both true, so clean drops to 0 one edge after the input falls.\n\nCausality: the defect produces a fault (cnt not cleared on the fall). That fault becomes a visible failure: a short low pulse of 2 edges reaches clean. The fault originates at the falling-edge clock, not at the cycle where a check later samples clean.\n\nIncorrectness: the restart condition should be `noisy != prev`, as the specification requires for both directions. That fix covers every short low glitch, not only this stimulus. Rising-edge behaviour is untouched by the defect, so short high pulses are still filtered.\n\nRanked hypotheses, each with the evidence that would refute it:\n(1) rtl_bug, falling edge does not restart the count. Refuted if the repro below passed on this RTL. It is supported by reading the RTL against its own specification comment.\n(2) testbench_bug, a wrong expectation in the triage repro. Refuted by deriving the expectation again from the spec clause. The new repro does that and checks only specified, implementation-independent behaviour. A filtered 2-edge pulse is well inside the 'STABLE edges or fewer' guarantee, and the long-hold checks allow 12 edges of settling. Rejected for the new repro. The triage testbench's content is not in my inputs, so I cannot independently judge its check.\n(3) infrastructure. Refuted by a clean build that reaches $finish with a counted verdict, which run-0002 reports ([evidence:prj-a26914b30e.triage.e2]). There is no sign of a build, tool or timeout problem. Rejected.\n(4) spec_ambiguity. Refuted if the clause failed to fix the behaviour. The clause explicitly says 'either direction' and 'high or low', so it is unambiguous for short low pulses. Rejected.\n\nRemaining uncertainty: the new repro's run has not been reported to me. Per the platform's gate, it is expected to fail on this RTL in check 2 only."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/debounce_rca_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: short low pulse must not reach clean", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the defect in [artifact:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-19189b08df]. It drives noisy on negative edges and applies 4 checks taken from the specification comment:\n(1) clean is 1 after a long high.\n(2) a 2-edge low pulse never reaches clean.\n(3) clean is 0 after a long low.\n(4) a 2-edge high pulse never reaches clean.\nOn the rise-only-restart RTL, check 2 is expected to fail. On RTL that restarts the count on either edge, all four are expected to pass. It reads the nonce with $value$plusargs and prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict just before $finish.", "entry": "debounce_rca_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["Reading the RTL, I expect check 2 of tb/debounce_rca_repro_tb.v to fail on debounce_rise_only_restart.v and checks 1, 3 and 4 to pass. This is not run or verified by me.", "I expect the same testbench to pass all four checks on an RTL whose restart condition is noisy != prev. This is not run or verified by me.", "The suggested fix is to replace `if (noisy && !prev)` with `if (noisy != prev)`. This is not applied or verified."], "escalation": null, "notes": "The independent review requirement still needs a review_record for this task. The design-under-investigation review ([evidence:prj-a26914b30e.design-under-investigation.e1]) covers the RTL, not this analysis. I did not see the triage testbench's source, so my rejection of testbench_bug rests on the new repro, whose expectations come from the spec."}
=== FILE: tb/debounce_rca_repro_tb.v ===
// Repro for prj-a26914b30e:root-cause.
// Specification (debounce header): a change on `noisy`, in either direction,
// restarts the count, so a pulse of STABLE edges or fewer, high or low, never
// reaches `clean`; a value held long enough does reach `clean`.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module debounce_rca_repro_tb;
    reg  clk   = 1'b0;
    reg  rst   = 1'b1;
    reg  noisy = 1'b0;
    wire clean;

    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;
    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    reg     bad;

    debounce #(.STABLE(4)) dut (
        .clk  (clk),
        .rst  (rst),
        .noisy(noisy),
        .clean(clean)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    initial begin
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
            nonce = "none";

        // Reset
        rst = 1'b1;
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (3) @(negedge clk);
        rst = 1'b0;

        // Check 1: a long high reaches clean
        noisy = 1'b1;
        repeat (12) @(negedge clk);
        if (clean === 1'b1) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK 1 FAILED: clean=%b after long high", clean);
        end

        // Check 2: a 2-edge low pulse must not reach clean
        bad = 1'b0;
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (2) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) bad = 1'b1;
        end
        noisy = 1'b1;
        repeat (10) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b1) bad = 1'b1;
        end
        if (!bad) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK 2 FAILED: a 2-edge low pulse reached clean");
        end

        // Check 3: a long low reaches clean
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (12) @(negedge clk);
        if (clean === 1'b0) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK 3 FAILED: clean=%b after long low", clean);
        end

        // Check 4: a 2-edge high pulse must not reach clean
        bad = 1'b0;
        noisy = 1'b1;
        repeat (2) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b0) bad = 1'b1;
        end
        noisy = 1'b0;
        repeat (10) begin
            @(negedge clk);
            if (clean !== 1'b0) bad = 1'b1;
        end
        if (!bad) passed = passed + 1;
        else begin
            failed = failed + 1;
            $display("CHECK 4 FAILED: a 2-edge high pulse reached clean");
        end

        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
